   static constexpr size_t REORDER = 16;
 
+  /*!
+   * \brief (Hades) For the times of a container that gives decoding times: how the difference
+   *        between the decoding times of the two tracks is learned
+   *
+   * At a base packet of a random-access picture, when the enhancement track has a packet of a
+   * random-access picture presented at the same time: that is the access unit of the base packet
+   * where the two layers have their pictures in the same order, and then so are the CONFIRM
+   * access units after it in each track, pairwise presented at the same times. Only then is the
+   * difference between the decoding times of the two packets taken (at most MAX_OFFSET seconds);
+   * the base packet waits for those packets where it is not the difference in use. Where the
+   * enhancement packet that it pairs with by the difference in use is no random-access one, the
+   * one of its picture may come later (an enhancement layer behind): the base packet waits for
+   * the enhancement packets of up to MAX_OFFSET seconds after it. Two layers
+   * coded in different orders (the two-track test stream of Hades: the same decoding times, and
+   * random-access pictures of the two layers at other access units, one of them presented at the
+   * time of one of the other layer) give no run of times, and nothing is learned. The difference
+   * stays after a seek (Clear(); it is checked again at the next such picture) and goes with
+   * Restart().
+   */
+  static constexpr size_t CONFIRM = 4;
+  static constexpr int MAX_OFFSET = 1;
+
   /*!
    * \brief After how many base packets without any enhancement packet the enhancement layer is
    *        silent
@@ -357,6 +397,11 @@ private:
     //! a packet of the enhancement track before its first random-access packet, where the times
